WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.987
(rockets blasting)

00:00:06.568 --> 00:00:08.985
(soft music)

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.160
- [Felicia] The events
of the past 24 hours

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.970
have been a serious test
for Israel's new government.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:23.970
You saw militants in Gaza,
launching incendiary balloons,

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.980
these are basically
balloons that are on fire

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.500
and aimed at setting ablaze

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.510
Israeli farms close to the Gaza border.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.493
That was in response to a rescheduled

00:00:36.493 --> 00:00:40.570
March through Jerusalem, where there were

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:44.450
some clashes between
Palestinians and police

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.934
leaving dozens injured.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.517
(upbeat music)

00:01:01.952 --> 00:01:04.702
(crowd chanting)

00:01:07.744 --> 00:01:11.827
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:01:15.439 --> 00:01:17.939
(soft music)

00:01:26.344 --> 00:01:30.410
I think both sides do have
some incentive not to escalate

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:31.890
but of course,

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.320
if another cycle of escalation
spirals out of control

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.770
with both sides trying
to prove themselves,

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:43.203
it could be a very volatile
and dangerous chapter.

00:01:44.821 --> 00:01:47.654
(crowds chanting)

